---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Us | UK Mountains Directory"
  description="Learn about UK Mountains Directory and our mission to provide comprehensive information about mountains across the United Kingdom."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="about-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>About UK Mountains Directory</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">
          Your comprehensive guide to exploring the mountains of the United Kingdom
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Our Mission</h2>
          <p>
            UK Mountains Directory is dedicated to providing accurate, comprehensive, and accessible information about
            every significant peak across England, Scotland, and Wales. Whether you're an experienced mountaineer
            planning your next Munro, a casual hiker looking for weekend adventures, or simply curious about the
            magnificent peaks that define our landscape, we're here to help.
          </p>
          <p>
            We believe that access to reliable mountain information should be free and available to everyone. Our mission
            extends beyond simply cataloging peaks - we aim to inspire a deeper appreciation for the UK's mountain heritage,
            promote safe and responsible mountain practices, and build a community of passionate mountain enthusiasts who
            respect and protect these natural treasures for future generations. Through detailed route information, historical
            context, and practical guidance, we empower adventurers of all levels to explore confidently and safely.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our team continuously researches and updates mountain data, working with local communities, conservation groups,
            and experienced mountaineers to ensure our information remains current and accurate. We're committed to environmental
            stewardship and encourage all visitors to follow Leave No Trace principles, respect wildlife habitats, and support
            local mountain communities. Together, we can preserve the beauty and integrity of UK mountains for generations to come.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>What We Offer</h2>
          <div class="features-grid">
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">⛰️</div>
              <h3>Comprehensive Database</h3>
              <p>
                Detailed information on Munros, Corbetts, Marilyns, and other significant peaks across the UK,
                including heights, locations, and classifications.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">📍</div>
              <h3>Location Services</h3>
              <p>
                Find mountains near you with our geolocation feature, complete with distances and directions to
                help plan your next adventure.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">🔍</div>
              <h3>Smart Search</h3>
              <p>
                Powerful search and filtering tools to help you find the perfect mountain based on region, height,
                classification, and more.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">📚</div>
              <h3>Rich Information</h3>
              <p>
                Discover the history, interesting facts, nearby facilities, and local attractions for each mountain
                to enhance your experience.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">🗺️</div>
              <h3>Route Planning</h3>
              <p>
                Detailed route descriptions with difficulty ratings, estimated times, elevation profiles, and
                turn-by-turn guidance to help you choose the perfect path.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">🌤️</div>
              <h3>Weather & Safety</h3>
              <p>
                Essential safety information, weather considerations, emergency contacts, and practical tips to
                ensure your mountain adventures are safe and enjoyable.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Mountain Classifications</h2>
          <div class="classifications">
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Munros</h3>
              <p>
                Scottish mountains over 3,000 feet (914.4 meters). Named after Sir Hugh Munro, who first cataloged
                them in 1891. There are 282 Munros in Scotland.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Corbetts</h3>
              <p>
                Scottish mountains between 2,500 and 3,000 feet (762-914 meters) with a drop of at least 500 feet
                on all sides. Named after John Rooke Corbett.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Marilyns</h3>
              <p>
                Mountains in the British Isles with a prominence of at least 150 meters (492 feet). The name is a
                pun on Munro, with the M representing "minimum" prominence.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Safety First</h2>
          <p>
            We believe that informed adventurers are safe adventurers. While we provide comprehensive information
            about each mountain, we always emphasize the importance of proper preparation, appropriate equipment,
            and respect for the natural environment.
          </p>
          <div class="safety-tips">
            <ul>
              <li>Always check weather forecasts before setting out</li>
              <li>Inform someone of your planned route and expected return time</li>
              <li>Carry appropriate equipment including maps, compass, and first aid kit</li>
              <li>Know your limits and choose routes appropriate for your fitness level</li>
              <li>Respect local guidelines and access restrictions</li>
              <li>Leave no trace - take your litter home</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
          <p>
            We are committed to maintaining accurate and up-to-date information about UK mountains. Our database
            is regularly updated to reflect changes in access, facilities, and other relevant information. If you
            notice any inaccuracies or have suggestions for improvements, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section cta-section">
          <h2>Start Exploring</h2>
          <p>
            Ready to discover the mountains of the UK? Start your journey today and find your next adventure.
          </p>
          <a href="/mountains" class="btn btn-primary">Explore Mountains</a>
        </section>

        <section class="faq-section content-section">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-container">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Who maintains UK Mountains Directory?</summary>
              <p>
                UK Mountains Directory is maintained by a dedicated team of mountain enthusiasts, experienced hillwalkers, and outdoor
                professionals who are passionate about UK mountains. We work closely with mountaineering organizations, conservation
                groups, and local communities to ensure our information is accurate and up-to-date.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>How do you ensure the accuracy of mountain information?</summary>
              <p>
                We use data from authoritative sources including Ordnance Survey, Scottish Mountaineering Club, and other recognized
                mountain organizations. Our team regularly reviews and verifies information, and we welcome feedback from users to help
                us maintain accuracy. When heights or classifications are updated by official bodies, we update our database accordingly.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Can I contribute information or photos?</summary>
              <p>
                Yes! We welcome contributions from the mountain community. If you have photos, route updates, or additional information
                about any UK mountain, please contact us through our contact page. While we can't guarantee all submissions will be used,
                we review each one carefully and appreciate community input in keeping our directory comprehensive and current.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Is UK Mountains Directory free to use?</summary>
              <p>
                Absolutely! UK Mountains Directory is completely free to access and use. We believe mountain information should be
                accessible to everyone. There are no hidden fees, subscriptions, or paywalls. Our goal is to support the mountain
                community by providing comprehensive, reliable information at no cost.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Do you cover mountains outside the UK?</summary>
              <p>
                Currently, UK Mountains Directory focuses exclusively on mountains in England, Scotland, and Wales. This allows us to
                provide the most detailed and accurate information possible for UK peaks. While we don't cover international mountains,
                we do include all significant UK peaks regardless of classification or height.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>How do I report incorrect information?</summary>
              <p>
                If you notice any incorrect or outdated information, please contact us through our contact page. Provide specific details
                about the error, including the mountain name and what needs correcting. We take accuracy seriously and will investigate
                and update information as quickly as possible. Your feedback helps us maintain the quality of our directory.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>Do you have a mobile app?</summary>
              <p>
                Currently, UK Mountains Directory is a web-based platform optimized for all devices including smartphones and tablets.
                Our responsive design ensures full functionality on mobile devices, so you can access mountain information on the go.
                We're exploring the possibility of a dedicated mobile app based on user feedback and interest.
              </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary>How often do you add new mountains to the directory?</summary>
              <p>
                We continuously expand our database to include more UK mountains. Priority is given to classified peaks (Munros, Corbetts,
                Marilyns, Wainwrights, etc.), but we're also adding prominent regional peaks. New mountains are added after thorough
                research to ensure comprehensive and accurate information. Check back regularly to discover newly added peaks.
              </p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
  }

  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);
    padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-3xl);
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .hero-text {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-3xl);
  }

  .content-section {
    background: white;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .content-section p {
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
  }

  .classifications {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .classification-item {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .classification-item h3 {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .classification-item p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
  }

  .safety-tips {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fef3c7 0%, #fde68a 100%);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .safety-tips ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .safety-tips li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-800);
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .cta-section .btn {
    background: white;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .cta-section .btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .faq-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .faq-item {
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    transition: all var(--transition-base);
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    transition: transform var(--transition-base);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .faq-item[open] summary::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .faq-item p {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .hero-text {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .content-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }

    .features-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
